{"chunk_id": "e47d85139f90", "text": "This section centers on the controversial intervention of Arjuna during Bhurisravas\u2019s near\u2011victory over Satyaki. As Bhurisravas drags the exhausted Satyaki by the hair and prepares to behead him, Krishna urges Arjuna to act. Arjuna shoots a razor\u2011headed arrow that severs Bhurisravas\u2019s arm. Outraged, Bhurisravas accuses Arjuna of violating the ethics of war by striking an opponent engaged with another. Arjuna counters that protecting an ally\u2014especially a disciple fighting for one\u2019s cause\u2014is a warrior\u2019s duty, and reminds him of the unjust killing of Abhimanyu. Bhurisravas then renounces battle and prepares for death through a yogic vow. Yet Satyaki, recalling his humiliation, beheads the meditating warrior, provoking widespread moral unease and debate over fate, vengeance, and dharma.\nArjuna saves Satyaki by severing Bhurisravas\u2019 arm, sparking a moral dispute, after which Satyaki kills the meditating, disarmed Bhurisravas.\nThemes: war ethics, loyalty and protection, revenge and vows, honor and shame, destiny versus choice", "vector": [0.00135397061239928, -0.015919411554932594, 0.0005761213251389563, 0.01298580877482891, 0.005268860142678022, 0.015563823282718658, -0.01434661727398634, -0.005959521979093552, -0.015221911482512951, -0.03293294087052345, 0.012678087688982487, 0.007686176337301731, 0.0003463993489276618, 0.0012351562036201358, -0.005115000065416098, 0.0018890624633058906, 0.05038411542773247, -0.00163262861315161, 0.03539470583200455, -0.02248411625623703, -0.012746470049023628, 0.005607352592051029, -0.004027720540761948, 0.01582367531955242, -0.01776573434472084, 0.03140117600560188, 0.002668621251359582, -0.03153793886303902, 0.011816469952464104, -0.030881470069289207, -0.018121322616934776, -0.0026959741953760386, -0.0009496599086560309, -0.006065514404326677, -0.03706323355436325, 0.0015779227251186967, 0.004403823520988226, -0.010462500154972076, 0.022032793611288